@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Dense stack-safe VF2 — data and control flow

rectangle "CodePropertyGraph\nexact typed multigraph" as CPG #DBE4FF
database "lazy dense node view\nascending NodeId\nunique in/out degree" as META #C3FAE8
rectangle "dense Vf2State\nu32 mapping arrays\nterminal counts" as STATE #E5DBFF
collections "Fenwick ordered sets\nunmapped · unused\npattern/target terminal" as SETS #D3F9D8
queue "search PDA\n(pattern index, cursor,\nterminal flag, ownership)" as SEARCH #FFF3BF
collections "flat undo logs\ncompact offset frames" as UNDO #FFE8CC
hexagon "kind + distinct degree +\nincident-edge feasible?" as FEASIBLE #FFE3E3
rectangle "PatternMatch\ncanonical NodeId mapping" as MATCH #D0EBFF

CPG --> META : first VF2 state only
META --> STATE : aligned ids and degrees
STATE --> SETS : membership / select
SETS --> SEARCH : first + next_at_or_after
SEARCH --> FEASIBLE : one candidate
META --> FEASIBLE : necessary degree bounds
CPG --> FEASIBLE : exact directed edges
FEASIBLE --> STATE : yes: push dense mapping
STATE --> UNDO : append changed indices
STATE --> MATCH : complete: emit
SEARCH --> UNDO : exhausted / capped: pop
UNDO --> STATE : exact inverse

note right of SEARCH
  Heap frames are defunctionalized
  continuations. Native call depth
  is constant in graph depth.
end note

note bottom of FEASIBLE
  Distinct degree is sound for the existing
  non-induced existential multiedge relation.
  Extra target edges remain permitted.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#DBE4FF>| authoritative graph |
  |<#C3FAE8>| lazy immutable metadata |
  |<#E5DBFF>| dense mutable search state |
  |<#D3F9D8>| ordered membership index |
  |<#FFF3BF>| pushdown control state |
  |<#FFE8CC>| exact restoration evidence |
  |<#FFE3E3>| feasibility decision |
  |<#D0EBFF>| immutable result |
endlegend
@enduml
